const sys=I.csys;const msgs=[{role:'user',content:'DEBATE TOPIC: '+I.topic+'\n\nThe defender opened:\n\n'+$('D1 Extract').first().json.raw+'\n\nChallenge this. Verse-level precision.'},{role:'assistant',content:$('C1 Extract').first().json.raw},{role:'user',content:'The defender responded:\n\n'+$('D2 Extract').first().json.raw+'\n\nFinal round. Close your challenge. Then END your response with a section titled exactly UNSUPPORTED-L4 PREMISES -- a numbered list (max 6) of the load-bearing [L4] inferences the DEFENDER\'s case relies on that were NOT exhibited through the prior layers (they float free of [L1]-[L3]). EACH NUMBERED LINE, AFTER ITS NUMBER, BEGINS WITH THE DECLARED CHAIN LINK IT ATTACKS, written exactly as LINK n: , where n is the number of that link in the defender\'s DECLARED CHAIN section; then name the inference and the defender claim it props. If a premise you name maps to NO declared link, write LINK none: and name it anyway -- it is judged, and an undeclared load-bearing premise counts against the defender\'s standing, but it is not counted in the chain length. EVERY premise must carry a verbatim quote of the defender\'s own words from the defender\'s earlier rounds -- the exact string, copied, not paraphrased -- and the premise may charge only what that quote says. After the quote, write PRESSED WITH: and every verse you pressed against that claim in your rounds, this one included, each by reference with its KJV words as you quoted them; write PRESSED WITH: none if you pressed none. Every verse you pressed against the defender\'s case in your rounds, this one included, is named on one of these numbered lines, beside the premise it was pressed against; a pressed verse left off the list is weaker: it reaches the judges only if the other side never names it. A pressed verse is a witness you carry, not a charge: it never widens what the premise charges. If you cannot quote the defender stating it, it is not the defender\'s premise and must not be listed. No commentary after the list. THEN, on its OWN LINE immediately after the list and nothing after it, write exactly: PREMISE COUNT: <number>, where <number> is how many premises you just listed. This is YOUR count of YOUR OWN list -- it is not the defender\'s chain length and it is never that number.'}];
